{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He saw the first portion for himself.</b> He saw to take for himself a portion in the land of Sihon and Og, for it is the first of the conquest of the land." "<b>For there the portion of.</b> For he knew that there, in his inheritance, is the <b>portion of</b> the burial-site of <b>the lawgiver</b> — and that is Moses (see Sifrei; Sotah 13)." "<b>Hidden.</b> That plot is סְפוּנָה and concealed from all creatures, as it is said ״וְלֹא יָדַע אִישׁ אֶת קְבֻרָתוֹ״ (Deuteronomy 34)." "<b>And he came.</b> Gad." "<b>The heads of the people.</b> They would go before the vanguard in the conquest of the land, for they were mighty, and so it says ״וְאַתֶּם תַּעַבְרוּ חֲמֻשִׁים לִפְנֵי אֲחֵיכֶם וְגוֹ׳״ (Joshua 1)." "<b>The righteousness of YHWH he performed.</b> They believed their words and kept their promise to cross the Jordan until they conquered and divided. Another interpretation — <b>And he came</b> Moses <b>at the head of the people, the righteousness of YHWH he performed</b> — said of Moses (see Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:52.797362815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}